On 2010-03-03, Spon <christoph.blau@gmail.com> wrote:
> This is a minor bug, if it even is one, but the .whereis file for each
> character (a tiny one-line text file that looks like it does exactly
> what it says on the tin) seems to be kept after a character's death.
> Is this intentional?  Is it safe to delete these files?

This is intentional -- on a multiplayer server, each person only ever
has a single character.  The .whereis file is then used to determine
where that player is or, posthumously, 'was'.

It is completely safe to delete these files.  Their only purpose is to
be read by an external program of your choice (I could, for example, see
someone writing a Windows app to track all characters currently 'in the
dungeon' for someone who switched between active ones frequently).

